{
  "uid": "cis-benchmark",
  "title": "CIS Kubernetes Benchmark — posture, and the tool that measures it",
  "tags": [
    "security",
    "cis",
    "compliance",
    "mdapi"
  ],
  "editable": true,
  "links": [],
  "refresh": "5m",
  "schemaVersion": 36,
  "timezone": "browser",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-30d",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "version": 1,
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "datasource",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "prometheus",
        "current": {
          "text": "Prometheus",
          "value": "Prometheus"
        },
        "hide": 0
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**The alert fires on regression from an accepted baseline, not on the existence of failures.** On a given distribution a share of the CIS items is not in your hands: they are decided by whoever owns the distribution. The architect's job is to separate what you fix from what you must require contractually, and to accept the remainder in writing.\n\n⭐ **Watch the failure curve for a step with no cause in the estate.** On 2026-09-20 this count went from 8 to 9 because Renovate upgraded kube-bench from v0.13.0 to v0.16.0 — proven by running both versions at the same moment on the same nodes. The net +1 hid a churn of **5 items out of 8**: two checks disappeared, three appeared. Compare the *lists*, never the totals.\n\nRe-deriving the set surfaced two settings genuinely unset on all three nodes — `protectKernelDefaults` and `rotateCertificates` — accepted, not clean, because the kubelet configuration belongs to the distribution. Baseline is pinned to the tool version in the alert rule itself."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Score",
      "description": "Passed over (passed + failed), identical on all three nodes — which is itself the evidence that the nodes are driven by code and not by hand.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "$datasource"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "max(kube_bench_score_ratio)",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 0.7
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0.85
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "decimals": 2
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Checks failing",
      "description": "Accepted baseline 9 under kube-bench v0.16.0. 7 are artefacts or accepted deviations, 2 are genuinely unset settings.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "$datasource"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "max(kube_bench_checks_fail)",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 10
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Checks passing",
      "description": "Automated checks the nodes satisfy.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "$datasource"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "max(kube_bench_checks_pass)",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "blue",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Last run succeeded",
      "description": "The weekly CronJob completed on every node. 0 means the posture shown is stale.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "$datasource"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "min(kube_bench_last_run_success)",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "0": {
                  "text": "NO",
                  "color": "red",
                  "index": 0
                },
                "1": {
                  "text": "YES",
                  "color": "green",
                  "index": 1
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Failures over time — a step here is usually the TOOL, not the estate",
      "description": "Before investigating a step, compare the running kube-bench image against the version named in the alert rule. A conformance threshold that is not versioned with the thing measuring it turns the next upgrade into an incident.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 9
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "$datasource"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "max(kube_bench_checks_fail)",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "failing"
        },
        {
          "expr": "max(kube_bench_checks_warn)",
          "refId": "B",
          "legendFormat": "warnings"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 5,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Failures by section and node — what is in your hands, and what is not",
      "description": "Section 1 is the control plane, section 4 the worker nodes. Identical counts across nodes mean a distribution-level deviation, not node drift.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 16
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "$datasource"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "kube_bench_section_fail > 0",
          "refId": "A",
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "transformations": [
        {
          "id": "organize",
          "options": {
            "excludeByName": {
              "Time": true,
              "__name__": true,
              "job": true,
              "prometheus": true,
              "service": true,
              "instance": true,
              "namespace": true,
              "endpoint": true,
              "container": true,
              "pod": true
            },
            "renameByName": {
              "node": "Node",
              "section": "Section",
              "Value": "Failing checks"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "sortBy",
          "options": {
            "sort": [
              {
                "field": "Failing checks",
                "desc": true
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "showHeader": true
      }
    }
  ]
}
